omotive industry we  can't afford to have the aluminum  industry collapse in this country it  wasn't just trade that had political  tongues wagging  last night President Trump met again  with the NRA leadership the second time  this week  the NRA s Chris Cox tweeting POTUS and V  POTUS don't want gun control the White  House insisted the president isn't  backtracking on his calls to improve gun  safety he just wants to hear from all  sides the president's made clear he  wants to talk to all of the big  stakeholders in this process he's spoken  with students with parents with teachers  with local law enforcement with state  and federal authorities as well as  members of the NRA he's going to  continue to have those conversations but  Democrats fear the momentum for change  is already fading Senator Chuck Schumer  saying in a statement President Trump  should go with his instincts not the  Clarion and destructive call of the NRA  if he continues to bow to his right-wing  Ringmaster's we will get nothing done on  guns and his presidency will continue to  fail and the controversy surrounding the  firing of former staff Secretary Rob  Porter  bubbled up again today when chief of  staff John Kelly filled in some blanks  for reporters at a pen and pad session  Kelly saying the first he heard about  allegations of spousal abuse was at  about 5:00 p.m. on Tuesday February 6th  involving Porter's second wife Kelly  went to see Porter who told him he'd  resigned about 90 minutes later after a  quick trip to Capitol Hill Kelley  learned of a second allegation this time  from Porter's first wife Porter assured  Kelly there was nothing to the  allegations but Kelly insisted Porter  had to resign that night and the next  day the White House released several  statements in support of Porter even  though he'd effectively been fired he is  going to be leaving the White House it  won't be immediate but he is resigning  from the White House but he's gonna stay  on to ensure that there's a smooth  transition moving forward  Kelly took the blame for that saying he  had not fully briefed the press office  on what had happened when he learned at  the photo of Porter's first wife with a  black eye he changed his statement to  condemn domestic abuse and revealed that  Porter had been removed from the White  House Kelly also said neither he nor  white House Counsel Don Magan were aware  the FBI had sent information about  Porter's security clearance file to the  White House in both March and July Kelly  told reporters today that he never  thought about resigning over the Porter  issue saying that he acted quickly when  he learned about it and did things as  appropriately as he thought he could  saying that there was nothing to  consider resigning over but Kelly did  acknowledge that the White House could  have handled the situation better  telling reporters quote we didn't cover  ourselves in glory in terms of how we  handled that on Wednesday morning it was  confusing  Brett John Roberts live in a windy North  Lawn John thanks

